{"assets":["/statement-assets/5c2f463a5523b4e220f29ed26ff73236cb665e7488ea51dc9a1459bc924d21dd.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"235","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B. Let's Play Osu!"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You're playing a game called Osu! Here's a simplified version of it. There are "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" clicks in a game. For each click there are two outcomes: correct or bad. Let us denote correct as \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", bad as \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"X"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", then the whole play can be encoded as a sequence of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" characters \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"X"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Using the play sequence you can calculate the score for the play as follows: for every maximal consecutive \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"s block, add the square of its length (the number of characters \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\") to the score. For example, if your play can be encoded as \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"OOXOOOXXOO"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", then there's three maximal consecutive \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"s block \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"OO"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"OOO"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"OO"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", so your score will be "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"22 + 32 + 22 = 17"},{"kind":"text","text":". If there are no correct clicks in a play then the score for the play equals to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You know that the probability to click the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(1 ≤ i ≤ n)"},{"kind":"text","text":" click correctly is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"pi"},{"kind":"text","text":". In other words, the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th character in the play sequence has "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"pi"},{"kind":"text","text":" probability to be \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 - pi"},{"kind":"text","text":" to be \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"X"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\". You task is to calculate the expected score for your play."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains an integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ n ≤ 105"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the number of clicks. The second line contains "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" space-separated real numbers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"p1, p2, ..., pn"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(0 ≤ pi ≤ 1)"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"There will be at most six digits after the decimal point in the given "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"pi"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print a single real number — the expected score for your play. Your answer will be considered correct if its absolute or relative error does not exceed "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"10 - 6"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3\n0.5 0.5 0.5\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2.750000000000000\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"4\n0.7 0.2 0.1 0.9\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2.489200000000000\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"r